{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 7.169,
   "text": "My grandmother had one rule about the farmhouse."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 7.769,
   "end": 13.657,
   "text": "Never answer the door after midnight. Not for the police. Not for family. Not even for her."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 14.257,
   "end": 17.628,
   "text": "She died in March. I moved in that June."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 18.328,
   "end": 23.832,
   "text": "For months, nothing happened. Then, on the first cold night of October, someone knocked."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 24.332,
   "end": 26.039,
   "text": "Three slow knocks."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 29.039,
   "end": 31.641,
   "text": "I didn't move. I didn't breathe."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 32.741,
   "end": 39.12,
   "text": "And then I heard her voice. Soft. Patient. Exactly the way she used to call me in from the yard."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 39.72,
   "end": 42.941,
   "text": "Sweetheart... it's cold out here. Let me in."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 44.341,
   "end": 52.597,
   "text": "My hand was already on the lock when I remembered the last thing she ever said to me, in the hospital, gripping my wrist so hard it bruised."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 53.297,
   "end": 56.327,
   "text": "When I'm gone... it will know my voice."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 58.927,
   "end": 61.359,
   "text": "That was eleven nights ago."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 62.959,
   "end": 66.159,
   "text": "Last night, it started using my mother's."
  }
 ],
